file: "packages/editor/src/pending/pending_banner.tsx"
doc: "The always-visible half of review: a count you can click to open the panel."

structs: [
  { name: "PendingBannerProps"
    doc:
      "`count` is how many proposals exist. `expanded` is whether the panel\n"
      "is currently open. `onToggle` is called with no arguments on click and\n"
      "on Enter or Space; the banner does NOT hold the expanded state, so it\n"
      "is the caller that flips it and passes it back down."
    fields: [
      { name: "count",    type: { primitive: INTEGER } },
      { name: "expanded", type: { primitive: BOOLEAN } },
      { name: "onToggle", type: { arrow: { output: { primitive: VOID } } } }
    ]
    typescript: { struct_kind: STRUCT_KIND_INTERFACE }
  }
]

constants: [
  { name: "PendingBanner"
    doc:
      "Renders NOTHING AT ALL when `count` is 0 -- not an empty bar. A file\n"
      "with no proposals is the normal case and must look untouched.\n"
      "\n"
      "With count >= 1 it renders one clickable strip reading '1 proposed\n"
      "change' when count is exactly 1 and '<count> proposed changes'\n"
      "otherwise, so the singular case is not '1 proposed changes'.\n"
      "\n"
      "Styled from the same island tokens the other floating surfaces use --\n"
      "--ag-panel, --ag-edge, --ag-radius, --ag-shadow -- so it reads as part\n"
      "of the same chrome family rather than as a browser notification.\n"
      "\n"
      "It is a <button>, not a div, and that is the WHOLE keyboard story: the\n"
      "component registers a click handler and NO keydown handler at all.\n"
      "Enter and Space reach onToggle through the browser's own synthesized\n"
      "click on a focused button. So one activation calls onToggle exactly\n"
      "once, and a bare keydown dispatched in a DOM test calls it zero times.\n"
      "`expanded` is reflected as aria-expanded.\n"
      "\n"
      "The ROOT CARRIES class=\"ag-island\", for the reason given on\n"
      "PendingPanel: IslandFrame's slots set pointer-events:none, it\n"
      "inherits, and a root without the class cannot be clicked at all.\n"
      "\n"
      "It is NOT given a slot of its own on IslandFrame, whose slot list is\n"
      "fixed. App puts it at the top of a column it passes into the existing\n"
      "inspector slot; what sits beneath it is App's decision, stated there."
    type: { named: { symbol: "Component", args: [{ named: { symbol: "PendingBannerProps" } }] } }
  }
]
